## 2. Consumer warpgroup ping-pong (warp-scheduler named barriers)

### Enum and **effective hardware barrier IDs**

User enum (`named_barrier.hpp`):

```50:58:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/named_barrier.hpp
enum class FwdNamedBarriers {
    QueryEmpty = 0,
    WarpSchedulerWG1 = 1,
    WarpSchedulerWG2 = 2,
    WarpSchedulerWG3 = 3,
    AppendKV = 4,
    QueryRotated = 5,
    PFull = 6,
    PEmpty = 7,
};
```

CUTLASS adds `FirstUserBarrier = 8` (`cutlass/arch/barrier.h:171`). All `NamedBarrier::sync/arrive(num_threads, user_id)` use **hardware ID = user_id + 8**:

| User enum | Hardware `bar.sync` / `bar.arrive` ID |
|-----------|----------------------------------------|
| `QueryEmpty` (0) | **8** |
| `WarpSchedulerWG1` (1) | **9** |
| `WarpSchedulerWG2` (2) | **10** |
| `WarpSchedulerWG3` (3) | **11** |
| `PFull` (6) | **14** |
| `PEmpty` (7) | **15** |

### When enabled

```367:371:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    static constexpr bool UseSchedulerBarrier = (IntraWGOverlap
        ? (NumMmaWarpGroups >= 2) && (!Is_FP8 ? kHeadDim <= 128 : kHeadDim >= 128)
        : NumMmaWarpGroups == 2)
        && !LargeHeadDimV;
```

Prefill hdim≤128 bf16 with `IntraWGOverlap=true` → **enabled**.

### Sync / arrive helpers

```952:988:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    warp_scheduler_barrier_sync() {
        if constexpr (UseSchedulerBarrier) {
            cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::sync(2 * cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup, static_cast<uint32_t>(FwdNamedBarriers::WarpSchedulerWG1) - 1 + flash::canonical_warp_group_idx_nosync() /*id*/);
        }
    }

    warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive() {
        if constexpr (UseSchedulerBarrier) {
            static_assert(NumMmaWarpGroups == 2 || NumMmaWarpGroups == 3);
            int const cur_WG = flash::canonical_warp_group_idx_nosync() - 1;
            int const next_WG = NumMmaWarpGroups == 2
                ? 1 - cur_WG
                : (cur_WG < NumMmaWarpGroups - 1 ? cur_WG + 1 : 0);
            cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::arrive(2 * cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup, static_cast<uint32_t>(FwdNamedBarriers::WarpSchedulerWG1) + next_WG /*id*/);
        }
    }
```

**Participant count:** always `256` threads (`2 × 128`) — both consumer warpgroups together.

**Ping-pong pattern (2 consumer WGs):**

| Consumer WG | Absolute WG idx | `sync` barrier (user → HW) | `arrive` barrier |
|-------------|-----------------|---------------------------|------------------|
| WG-A (first MMA) | 1 | `WarpSchedulerWG1` → **9** | `WarpSchedulerWG2` → **10** |
| WG-B (second MMA) | 2 | `WarpSchedulerWG2` → **10** | `WarpSchedulerWG1` → **9** |

Each WG **syncs on its own barrier** and **signals the peer’s barrier** → one-phase offset.

**Bootstrap** (WG-A starts the chain):

```981:987:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        if constexpr (UseSchedulerBarrier) {
            if (warp_group_idx == 1) {
                cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::arrive(2 * cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarpGroup, static_cast<uint32_t>(FwdNamedBarriers::WarpSchedulerWG1) /*id*/);
            }
        }
```

### Placement in mainloop (`IntraWGOverlap` `fwd_step`)

Per inner iteration (`n_block` loop), order is:

```1244:1280:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
            auto fwd_step = [&](int const n_block, auto mask_fn, auto check_inf_type) {
                PipelineState smem_pipe_read_v(smem_pipe_read.index(), smem_pipe_read.phase(), smem_pipe_read.count());
                ++smem_pipe_read;
                ...
                if (!UseSchedulerBarrier || warp_group_idx == 0) { consumer_wait(pipeline_k, smem_pipe_read); }
                warp_scheduler_barrier_sync();                                    // (A) ping-pong enter
                flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/true, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_qk, ...);  // QK(i)
                if constexpr (RescaleOBeforeGemm) { softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale); }
                if (!UseSchedulerBarrier || warp_group_idx == 0) { consumer_wait(pipeline_v, smem_pipe_read_v); }
                flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/false, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_pv, ...); // PV(i-1)
                warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive();                                // (B) ping-pong exit — peer may WGMMA
                warpgroup_wait<1>();
                pipeline_k.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read);
                ...
                scoremod_premask_fn(tSrS);
                mask_fn(tSrS, n_block);
                ... online_softmax ...
                warpgroup_wait<0>();
                pipeline_v.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read_v);
                ... write P ...
                if constexpr (!RescaleOBeforeGemm) { softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale); }
```

**Interpretation:**
- **Between (A) and QK issue:** this WG waits until peer finished its prior WGMMA batch → peer is free to run **softmax** while this WG issues **QK+PV**.
- **At (B):** this WG has **issued** both GEMMs (not finished) → peer can enter (A) and start its QK.
- **After (B):** this WG runs **softmax on QK(i)** while peer’s WGMMAs are in flight.
- Only **relative `warp_group_idx == 0`** (first consumer WG) calls `consumer_wait` on K/V when scheduler barrier is on — pipeline waits are centralized on one WG; the other relies on ping-pong timing.

**Non-`IntraWGOverlap` path** (serial QK → softmax → PV per WG, but still ping-pong across WGs):

```1353:1393:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
                consumer_wait(pipeline_k, smem_pipe_read);
                flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/true, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_qk, ...);
                warp_scheduler_barrier_arrive();   // after QK — peer can softmax
                warpgroup_wait<0>();
                pipeline_k.consumer_release(...);
                ... softmax, write P ...
                consumer_wait(pipeline_v, smem_pipe_read);
                warp_scheduler_barrier_sync();     // before PV — wait for peer
                flash::gemm</*zero_init=*/false, /*wg_wait=*/-1>(tiled_mma_pv, ...);
```

